{"Backup-code branch bypasses TOTP requirement when disabling 2FA - the handler accepts backupCode as an alternate path that runs before TOTP validation and doesn't require a valid TOTP code, allowing any authenticated session with password to disable 2FA using a backup code": 0.22139374911785126, "Used backup code is never invalidated when disabling 2FA, allowing a stolen code to be reused until the account is reconfigured": 0.06377193331718445, "Backup codes are persisted to database during setup before 2FA is actually enabled, creating a data-model lifecycle mismatch where backup codes exist for accounts not yet protected by 2FA": 0.25105899572372437, "Backup-code login submit button lacks isSubmitting guard, allowing double-click or Enter-key repeat to send two credential requests before first response returns, causing spurious IncorrectBackupCode errors": 0.2648976743221283, "Backup codes can be reused indefinitely during login - the authorizeCredentials path sets matched entry to null but the code may remain accepted depending on how the array is interpreted later": 0.20219437777996063, "Stale backup-code download URL may point to old code set - opening modal multiple times can leave prior object URLs alive because cleanup is not tied to backupCodesUrl changes in effect lifecycle": 0.3021366596221924, "2FA enable flow no longer calls onEnable when 2FA is actually enabled on server - callback is now delayed until modal is dismissed instead of immediately after server returns 200": 0.8715400695800781, "Mode switching between TwoFactor and BackupCode can leave stale totpCode/backupCode values in submitted form, causing hidden leftover backup code to override visible TOTP entry due to auth layer preferring credentials.backupCode when present": 0.7392112612724304}